      "writtenOn": "2026-09-10T20:56:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done, as change 8393057: it reverts 01a78fbc and returns -1 from vpx_img_set_rect() when the image is flipped, with a test covering both of the cases that commit handled, a non-empty rectangle and an empty one.\n\nThe caller audit agrees with restricting it. After the revert vpx_img_flip() has no caller outside its own tests, and the only live vpx_img_set_rect() call in the tree is the whole-image one inside img_alloc_helper(), which runs before anything could flip the image. The call in vp8_cx_iface.c is inside a comment block. libaom is the same shape, where aom_img_flip() has no caller at all, so I have uploaded the matching change there as patch set 5 of 216401.\n\nThat leaves what this change was about. vpx_img_flip() on an image allocated with a zero dimension does not go through vpx_img_set_rect(), and it still offsets the planes by UINT_MAX rows because d_h - 1 is computed in unsigned int. If you would rather restrict that as well, the equivalent is vpx_img_alloc() rejecting a zero width or height, and I am happy to upload that and abandon this one. Whichever you prefer.",
      "parentUuid": "525379b4_8d937e70",
      "revId": "5eaa89f34c8b26f6e4ebf8675053c28d28e56640",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
